From: 24bit192kHz <118996408+24bit192kHz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] [local] pci_rom: bound CBFS probe and ACPI image copies

Carry the actual decompressed cbfs_map length through ID fallback and the
ACPI _ROM copy. Validate bounded header/PCIR metadata before dereferencing
it, and require a complete bounded image chain rather than enlarging the
copy to an unchecked legacy init length. Preserve all nonpadding bytes of
the valid MX150 image (182272 bytes).

Source-only proposal after 0029, not installed firmware. Baseline coreboot
c57exp 84126e3fc1e4129f5be9af44d633736cea68d169, src/device/pci_rom.c SHA-256
9770b6345ab1d15e74cb43e06691a0dbc5080ed6c874c7dbcb4fd92ebc025b24.
The complete correction includes following patch 0031, which fixes cbfs_map
size_out to report actual produced bytes rather than declared allocation
capacity. cbfs_get_size reports stored length and is not this mapping bound.
Keep the strict image walker inside HAVE_ACPI_TABLES for non-ACPI builds.

Unknown on-device ROM mappings and already-loaded executable RAM ROMs are
not newly bounded by this change. Generic pci_rom_load execution/copy and
VFCT contracts are not claimed repaired. Strict _ROM validation rejects
incomplete CBFS PCI image chains; a valid x86 init-prefix artifact alone
is not a complete image fixture for that contract.

---
